-- R2: one binder per name. A rule's own GIVEN may not restate a name a section
-- GIVEN already binds -- after discharge the binder is a parameter of every
-- rule that reads it, so the restatement would give one name two binders.
--
-- The fix is to delete the restatement, at which point the section's value
-- flows in; a genuine per-call variation is written `callee WITH x IS y`.

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN `the rate` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
restated MEANS `the rate` TIMES 2
